                        <item_1570890140330
                            cq:panelTitle="Itinerary"
                            jcr:lastModified="{Date}2020-07-08T15:33:47.780-07:00"
                            jcr:lastModifiedBy="admin"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="weekender/components/contentfragment"
                            displayMode="singleText"
                            elementNames="itinerary"
                            fragmentPath="/content/dam/weekender-shared/en/adventures/beervana-portland/beervana-in-portland"
                            paragraphScope="all"
                            text="Beervana in Portland We meet at eleven in the inner east side, a district of old warehouses that brewers moved into twenty years ago. Morning: how beer is made The first stop is a working brewhouse. Among the tanks we look at malt, hops, yeast and water, smell and taste each of them, and follow a batch from grain to glass. The tasting that follows covers the main families of beer, from a pale lager to a dark stout. Lunch: food and beer together A short walk brings us to a brewery with a kitchen. The cook pairs four small plates with four beers and explains each choice. Afternoon: the experiments The last two stops are tiny. One ages its beers in wine barrels, the other brews with fruit from farms nearby. We finish by five, close to a tram stop."
                            variationName="master">
